WEBVTT

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.130
Godai as a teacher

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.130
I can't imagine it.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.270
Teaching at an all-girls school?
I'd love to do it myself.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.310
Don't get involved
with your students.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.910
Are you really qualified?

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.540
It's none of your business!!

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.220
Leave me alone!

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.320
C'mon, teacher. Loosen up.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.580
That's right. They'll hate
a crabby teacher like you.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.820
Cut it out!!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.730
M-Manager.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.030
Have we done something wrong?

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.630
Godai starts
student teaching tomorrow!

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.200
That's why we're here
to cheer him on.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.860
Here. Have a drink.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.380
It looks to me like
you're just bothering him.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.640
Isn't he teaching
at your alma mater?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.610
Uh-huh.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.380
Where your husband was?

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.320
Right.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.730
W-What?

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.320
That's right.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.890
They turned you down as a student
teacher at the rural school?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.790
Well, I sent in
my application too late.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.160
All right. I'll put in
a good word for you.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.950
R-Really?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.880
Leave it to me.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.600
That's how I got
Soichiro into teaching.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.730
Mr. Otonashi is a trustee
at an all-girls school.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.700
The very school...

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.450
where the manager
and her husband had met.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.310
That's where I'll
be student teaching.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:00.890
I'm off!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.450
Bye!

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.130
I hope he'll be all right.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.100
He didn't sleep at all, did he?

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:12.200
He'll be fine. He's still young.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:21.570
But it takes quite a bit of stamina
to keep high-school girls in line.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.270
SOICHIRO OTONASHI

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.860
Uh... I will be your
Earth Science teacher.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.080
My name is Mr. Otonashi.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.570
He seems like a quiet guy.
I wonder if he'll be okay?

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.810
Mr. Otonashi, do you
have a girlfriend?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.570
N-No...Women...don't seem...to be

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:54.840
attracted to me.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.640
- What an answer.
- You're so mean to ask.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.820
So...

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.760
Shall we...start the class?

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.150
Oh, boy.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.240
Hey! Be quiet, everyone!

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.630
Thank you...very much.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.610
Sure. It's my job as
the class president.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:25.510
I see.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.380
Mr. Otonashi, our class
is always like this.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.250
I think you better
speak more loudly.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.880
I'll keep that in mind.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.670
He didn't seem like a teacher...

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.680
My Soichiro.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:11.190
I'm here to introduce
Mr. Godai, a student teacher.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.200
Quiet down, ladies.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.590
Please, Mr. Godai.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.110
Y-Yes.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.550
U-Uh...

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.080
M-My name is Yusaku Godai.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.780
F-For the n-next two weeks–

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.630
Hey! Be quiet, everyone!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.470
Th-Thank you.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.590
Sure. It's my job as
the class president.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.950
I see. Class president.
She's pretty cute.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:18.250
S-So, I'll be conducting
your literature class.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:19.450
Question!

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.870
Mr. Godai, do you have
a girlfriend?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.960
Quiet! Let him answer.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.760
So? Do you, Mr. Godai?

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.070
U-Uh...Well...

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.030
Let's see...
A girlfriend...

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.050
How can I put it... Well...

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.550
Don't have to take it
so seriously.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:01.070
You should have more confidence.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.860
I'm sorry. I was overwhelmed.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:09.400
Male teachers are a novelty here,
so the girls get excited.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.260
He seems so naive.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.580
There's something charming
about his scrawniness.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:27.220
He's got sort of a melancholy look.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:29.940
Melancholy? That's not it.

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.960
He's just gloomy, that's all.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.270
These girls are crazy.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.940
Is this normal at
an all-girls school?

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.960
Because there're few men?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.180
Is that why the manager–

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.520
Mr. Otonashi.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.970
I wonder what Soichiro...

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:57.850
...her husband, was like?

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:02.320
The yearbook!

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.890
Manager!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:38.430
Her photos are everywhere.
She must have been popular.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.320
Oops!. I came to see
a photo of her husband.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.230
We got another lame-o.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:50.870
Our school must be a magnet
for loser male teachers.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.550
Why can't we get
someone cool for once?

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.540
Yagami, would you please go get
the slides for the next class?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.190
All right.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:06.320
Otonashi...Otonashi.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.320
There's quite a few teachers.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:12.990
Oh no...!

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.940
SOICHIRO OTONASHI

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.810
Why couldn't he just ask
the slide monitor?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:33.950
Oh?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.690
Mr. Godai?

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:42.850
What's he doing in
a dark place like this?

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.440
I'm such a fool...

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.810
dwelling on someone
who's been dead.

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:02.080
W-What did he mean by that?

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.040
Who died?

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.350
Uh-oh. I'm getting sleepy.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:31.030
You're–

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.100
I'm Yagami.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.150
Tears?!

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.620
Oh!. I was just yawning.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.290
I was up all night last night.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.250
Were you watching
all this time?

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:53.800
No.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.750
Please...

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:56.750
Yes?

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.670
Don't tell anyone
you saw me here.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:03.570
Sure. It'll be our secret.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.150
Looking through
a yearbook, tear-eyed?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:15.910
His girlfriend
must have passed away.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.350
She must have gone
to this school.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:23.350
No wonder he's a melancholy man.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.730
Are you serious, Yagami?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.910
I thought you had no interest.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.680
You said he's just gloomy.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:49.240
I've changed my mind.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.970
You did, huh?

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.660
It only took you half a day.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:55.900
Bye!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.060
Bye!

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:01.230
Well then, good luck to you.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:03.730
Thanks!

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:05.830
See ya!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.040
Mr. Godai!

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:19.070
Bye! Cheer up!

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.210
W-What was that?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.290
Boy, that hurt.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.400
I guess high-school pranks
haven't changed much.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.030
Kyoko! There goes Mr. Otonashi.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:16.140
C'mon! Hurry! He's leaving!

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.480
- Kyoko, you chicken!
- Scaredy cat!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.620
How childish I was then, trying to
express my feelings like that.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:43.820
But...

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.000
I wonder what kind
of girl did this?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:52.180
["Kokoro" by Soseki Natsume]
After that day, I began to visit
Sensei at regular intervals.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.080
I found him always at home.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:58.570
And the more I visited Sensei...

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:02.840
the more eager I became
to see him again.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.550
Okay. Good.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.450
Takada, please read from there.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.430
Yes.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:11.300
Despite this, however...

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:20.740
there was no great change in
Sensei's manner towards me.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.570
W-What? She keeps staring at me!

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.190
W-What?

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.720
Hey! Are you really serious?

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:45.220
I didn't know you like
the "loser" type.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.330
He's not a loser.

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:52.910
He's coping with a tragic past.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:54.820
Huh?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.970
What tragic past?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.940
Oh, nothing.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:06.080
Well, if you're serious, Yagami,

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:10.060
you better do something while
he's here as a student teacher.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.480
I know.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:16.890
I want make him happy over time.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.240
Mr. Godai!

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.560
Going home already?

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:48.300
Y-Yes. You, too?

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:52.230
Great. We'll walk
with you halfway.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:54.590
Huh?

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.720
Welcome back.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.640
H-Hi.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.680
No way! Isn't this
a boarding house?!

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.560
I can't believe it!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.890
There still ARE boarding houses.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.210
Are they students
from your class?

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.260
Y-Yes.

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.650
Hello!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.350
You've made quite a few friends.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:21.400
N-No. They just followed me here.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.530
Hey! Who's that?

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.440
She's beautiful.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.760
She must be a tenant here.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.200
Why don't you have them
come inside?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.060
May I?

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:36.800
That's up to you! It's your room.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.770
I-I guess so.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:44.470
Why is Mr. Godai
acting nervous like that?

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:46.860
Would you like to come inside
for a little while?

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:49.160
Really? Can we?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:50.450
Well, then.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.290
Thank you!

00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:59.520
Why is Godai
acting nervous like that?

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.500
It's a mess, but
make yourselves at home.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.870
A mess? There's nothing here.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.910
I-I guess.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:15.500
This room has
absolutely no personality.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.890
High...school...girls...?

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:22.400
Snake man!!

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.090
Mr. Godai, who's this?!

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.660
Don't make eye contact!!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.890
Yotsuya! You know–

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.790
Godai, are you kicking me out?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.770
I only came to say hello.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:37.410
Thank you for
looking after Godai.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.410
N-No problem.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:43.240
I'm like an older
brother to him.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.800
Really?

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.650
He couldn't do
anything without me.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:49.800
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:53.650
- Yes?
- I brought some juice.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.310
So you're Godai's students?

00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:01.490
Bringing girls home on your
first day? Way to go, teacher.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.790
Akemi!

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.950
My gosh. That's
totally see-through.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.700
How slutty.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.730
Is Mr. Godai all right here?

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.630
Huh?

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:12.030
Here you go.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:16.230
You shouldn't have, Manager.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.150
So she's the manager.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:23.410
Why's he so nice to her?

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.150
By the way, Godai...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:34.700
I think I got that red heart
out of your dress shirt.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.400
Thank you so much.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:42.000
Wow! The manager does
the tenants' laundry here?

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:45.760
No. Godai gets
special treatment.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:49.110
She's unfairly nice to Godai.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.940
That's not true.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.450
Do you manage this place alone?

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.710
You have a husband, don't you?

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.120
She's a widow!

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.600
A widow?

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.200
If she's a widow
she's available, right?

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.490
It's suspicious.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:18.910
I agree.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:22.770
A widow and her tenant.
How cliché.

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:26.540
And she does his laundry?
That's not normal.

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.080
They're an item.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.090
I'm sure.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:31.910
What're you gonna do, Yagami?

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:33.350
Are you going to give up?

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.400
Why should I?

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.390
You're just assuming
that they're an item.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:39.950
But...

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.490
What matters is how Mr. Godai feels.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.830
Besides, she's a widow!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.440
Of course a high-school girl
is way better than a widow!

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:48.660
Why?

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.720
Who says?

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.840
I don't know!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:57.410
How dare she, anyway?!
I put that heart there!

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:28.940
Please! If it works out
I'll treat you to anything!!

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.870
I want you to capture
the perfect moment!

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:41.000
Mr. Godai.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.090
Yes?

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:46.400
Um... I have to talk to you.

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:49.220
W-What is it?

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.530
Thanks for having us yesterday.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:55.760
No problem. I didn't
have much to offer.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.720
I have strange neighbors.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:59.140
Mr. Godai!

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:03.700
Are you mad that
we went to your place?

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:06.890
N-No. It was fun.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.240
Really?

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:09.500
Yeah.

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.380
Yay! I'm so glad!

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:29.870
- Did you get it?
- Got it!

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:33.330
Not bad for a Polaroid.

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:34.410
Right?

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:36.040
What're you gonna do with it?

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.530
I have a plan.

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:41.350
Express Delivery!

00:22:41.480 --> 00:22:44.450
Yes! Thank you.

00:22:51.460 --> 00:22:52.510
For me?

00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:57.090
What could it be?

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:03.290
I get it.

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:07.030
A proclamation of war.

00:23:16.720 --> 00:23:18.710
As it says here,

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:23.220
the author lived an idealistic
individualistic life

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:27.520
and later in life, he wrote
about the human egoism.

00:23:27.790 --> 00:23:31.050
And in the last years of his life,
he changed his views.

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:34.590
He abandoned all his ego and
tried to view the world–

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:48.580
What are you doing, Yagami?!

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:51.940
We'll both be in trouble
if someone sees us like this!

00:23:52.150 --> 00:23:54.620
Am I that unattractive?

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:58.420
Next: "Barefaced Attack!
Operation Seduction"

00:23:58.490 --> 00:24:02.180
High-school girls today
are pretty bold!
